## Fix: Complex Rule assistant — "[object Object]" reply and unusable "Something else" option

### Context
In the Complex Rule builder chat, the agent offered "Something else (let me explain)"
as a clickable option. Clicking it sent that literal text as the answer, the user had no
way to type, and the agent's next reply rendered as `[object Object],[object Object]`.
Root cause: some serving endpoints (Claude-style) return `message.content` as a list of
blocks. The engine stored that list as `reply`, which the browser stringified; the list
also went back in `history`, where the backend silently drops non-string content, so the
agent lost its own previous question and answered without context.

### Changes
1. `src/agents/engine_base.py` — new shared `normalize_reply_content` / `UNREADABLE_REPLY`
   (moved from the Graph Chat engine) that flattens content blocks into Markdown text.
2. `src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/engine.py` — now imports the shared helper (behaviour unchanged).
3. `src/agents/agent_complex_rule_builder/engine.py` — normalise the LLM content so `reply`
   is always a string; prompt now forbids catch-all options ("Something else"/"Other").
4. `src/agents/agent_complex_rule_builder/tools.py` — `propose_options` coerces object
   options to labels, de-duplicates, and drops catch-all answers.
5. `src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-business-rules.js` + `.../css/ontology-business-rules.css`
   — every option group gets a built-in "Something else…" pill that focuses the chat input
   instead of sending text.
6. `tests/units/agents/test_agent_complex_rule_builder.py` — tests for block-list content
   and option sanitising.

### Modified files
